.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt OPENCODE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm opencode
.Nd OpenCode, a coding agent for the terminal
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -standalone
.Op Fl -auto
.Op Ar directory
.Nm
.Cm run
.Op Fl -standalone
.Op Fl -auto
.Op Fl m Ar provider/model
.Op Ar message ...
.Nm
.Cm auth login
.Op Fl -method Ar id
.Op Ar integration
.Nm
.Cm service
.Cm start | stop | status
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is OpenCode: an agent that reads and changes the files of a directory and
runs commands there, at the request of a person or of a model it talks to
on a provider's service, such as OpenAI, Anthropic or OpenCode's own.
With no command it draws its screen and takes requests one after another;
.Cm run
sends one message without the screen and prints the answer.
.Ql opencode --help
lists the commands, and
.Ql opencode Ar command Fl -help
describes one.
.Pp
The x86-64 GNU root has
.Nm
when it is built with the agents layer:
.Ql make ARCH=x86_64 GNU_AGENTS=opencode os-real-gnu-ext2 ,
or
.Ql GNU_AGENTS=all ,
which the release to the installed machine uses.
The program is the project's own build of version 2.2.5 for
linux-x64-baseline, one executable of 253 MB that holds Bun, a JavaScript
runtime, with its scripts and native libraries, installed unmodified as
.Pa /opt/opencode/bin/opencode .
.Pa /usr/bin/opencode
and
.Pa /bin/opencode
link to it.
Its license, MIT, is
.Pa /opt/opencode/LICENSE .
.Ss Signing in over SSH
.Ql opencode auth login
asks which integration to connect and by which method, unless the command
line names them.
Each of the methods below works from an SSH session, with no browser on
this machine.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It ChatGPT, by a device code
.Ql opencode auth login openai --method chatgpt-headless ,
which the menu calls
.Dq Codex device code ,
prints the address
.Lk https://auth.openai.com/codex/device
and a one-time code.
Enter the code at that address on any other computer, signed in to a
ChatGPT account whose security settings allow sign-in by a device code.
The method the menu calls
.Dq Sign in with ChatGPT
instead waits for a web browser to return to a server that
.Nm
runs on this machine's loopback interface, which a browser on another
computer cannot reach.
.It OpenCode's console, by a device code
.Ql opencode auth login opencode --method device
prints a one-time code and an address at
.Lk https://opencode.ai/console/device
that carries it; open the address on any other computer, sign in there and
approve the request.
.It An API key
.Ql opencode auth login anthropic ,
or another provider's name, asks for the provider's key on the terminal
and stores it.
A key in the provider's environment variable, such as
.Ev ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
or
.Ev OPENAI_API_KEY ,
is used without being stored.
.El
.Pp
.Ql opencode auth list
lists the integrations signed in,
.Ql opencode auth logout
removes one, and
.Ql opencode models
lists the models they offer.
OpenCode's own provider offers a few free models with no sign-in.
.Ss Where the credentials live
.Nm
keeps every credential, API keys and the tokens of a sign-in alike, in
plain text in its database,
.Pa ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db ,
a SQLite database with mode 0600 in WAL mode, which holds its sessions as
well; treat the file, with its
.Pa -wal
and
.Pa -shm
files beside it, as a password.
.Ev XDG_DATA_HOME
names another directory in place of
.Pa ~/.local/share ,
and
.Ev OPENCODE_DB
another database.
.Ql opencode auth export
prints the stored credentials, secrets included, as JSON, and
.Ql opencode auth import
reads them back, on this machine or another.
.Ss The background service
As shipped,
.Nm
runs its sessions in a server shared by every client of the user: the
screen,
.Cm run ,
.Cm auth
and the other commands that need a session connect to it, and start it as
.Ql opencode serve --service
when it is not running.
The service listens on a port of the loopback interface, 127.0.0.1, which
it names in
.Pa ~/.local/state/opencode/service.json ,
takes the password it keeps in
.Pa ~/.config/opencode/service.json ,
mode 0600, and outlives the client that started it, until
.Ql opencode service stop
ends it.
.Ql opencode service status
prints its address, or
.Ql stopped .
.Pp
.Fl -standalone
runs a private server for one client instead, as a child that ends with
it, and leaves no process behind.
.Fl -server Ar url
connects to another server.
.Ss Permissions and the sandbox
.Nm
has no sandbox: the commands the model asks for, and its edits, run with
every right of the user who runs it.
Its permission settings decide which tools it asks about before using;
.Fl -auto
approves every request that the settings do not deny.
Run
.Nm
as an ordinary user, on files that the work can afford to change.
.Ss Updates
.Pa /etc/profile.d/opencode.sh
sets
.Ev OPENCODE_DISABLE_AUTOUPDATE
to 1 in every login shell, which keeps
.Nm
from asking
.Lk https://opencode.ai
for a newer release at its start; a command that
.Xr ssh 1
runs without a login shell does not have it.
.Ql opencode upgrade
fails here, since it finds none of the installers it knows in
.Pa /opt/opencode ;
a new version comes with a new build of the root.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev OPENCODE_DISABLE_AUTOUPDATE
1 or true turns off the check for a newer release.
.It Ev OPENCODE_DB
the database in place of
.Pa ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db .
.It Ev OPENCODE_DISABLE_MODELS_FETCH
1 or true keeps the catalog of models from being fetched.
.It Ev TMPDIR
where Bun unpacks the native libraries of the program at each start, or
.Pa /tmp .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /opt/opencode/bin/opencode
the program
.It Pa /opt/opencode/LICENSE
its license
.It Pa /etc/profile.d/opencode.sh
turns off the update check
.It Pa ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db
the credentials and the sessions
.It Pa ~/.local/share/opencode/log/
the logs of each start
.It Pa ~/.config/opencode/
a person's settings and the service's password
.It Pa ~/.local/state/opencode/service.json
the running service's address and process
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 on success and 1 on an error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Sign in to ChatGPT from an SSH session, then ask for one change in the
current directory without the screen and with no service left behind:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ opencode auth login openai --method chatgpt-headless
$ opencode run --standalone "Fix the failing test in tests/parse.sh"
.Ed
.Pp
End the background service that the screen started:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ opencode service stop
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr claude 1 ,
.Xr codex 1 ,
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr tmux 1
.Pp
.Lk https://opencode.ai/docs "The OpenCode documentation"
